WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.010 --> 00:10.010
=Watch on kissasia.biz or asiankh.org=

3
01:10.613 --> 01:12.321
Let's go.

4
01:19.061 --> 01:22.453
You really had no idea Hongsung had teamed up with Mantua?

5
01:22.453 --> 01:25.449
No, I never saw it coming.

6
01:25.449 --> 01:27.633
Look at you bragging.

7
01:27.633 --> 01:29.233
What's going to happen to us?

8
01:29.233 --> 01:31.400
What do you mean, what's going to happen?

9
01:31.400 --> 01:33.813
We used to do business with Hongsung.

10
01:33.813 --> 01:36.053
We're just going back to the way things were.

11
01:36.053 --> 01:38.033
Nothing's changing.

12
02:43.225 --> 02:52.233
[Episode 10, Even A Lottery Winner Still Goes to Work]

13
03:04.833 --> 03:06.893
Thank you.

14
03:06.893 --> 03:10.497
I can't remember the last time we sat down together like this.

15
03:10.497 --> 03:13.797
Neither can I. When was it?

16
03:13.797 --> 03:17.209
I think it was when you were at the Pyeongtaek branch.

17
03:17.209 --> 03:19.877
Oh, I suppose it was.

18
03:19.877 --> 03:22.813
That was when you came to the Pyeongtaek branch,

19
03:22.813 --> 03:26.933
and turned the place upside down, threatening to pull all Hongsung's stores.

20
03:28.489 --> 03:31.077
Oh, I was shaking in my boots that day.

21
03:31.077 --> 03:36.100
You kept shouting about pulling the brand out and complaining to headquarters.

22
03:36.100 --> 03:38.085
You were so loud

23
03:38.085 --> 03:41.073
that we ended up getting complaints from customers, remember?

24
03:41.073 --> 03:43.277
They said it was too noisy to shop.

25
03:43.277 --> 03:46.141
Did you know headquarters booked the room next to the restaurant?

26
03:46.141 --> 03:47.377
Pardon?

27
03:47.377 --> 03:51.601
A stenographer will record the minutes and send them straight to the chairman.

28
03:51.601 --> 03:54.566
That's how important this meeting is.

29
03:54.566 --> 03:56.689
Oh, you were there too, weren't you?

30
03:56.689 --> 03:59.025
Yes, I was there.

31
03:59.025 --> 04:03.429
After Mr. Hong left, you came back for the working-level talks,

32
04:03.429 --> 04:04.981
didn't you, Mr. Jang?

33
04:04.981 --> 04:07.065
Oh, yes. That's correct.

34
04:07.065 --> 04:08.109
You remember.

35
04:08.109 --> 04:11.166
I retrained our staff after that incident.

36
04:11.166 --> 04:13.493
"Don't you dare mess with Hongsung, got it?"

37
04:13.493 --> 04:17.133
"Nothing good comes from crossing them, nothing at all."

38
04:18.733 --> 04:23.853
Oh, by the way, you heard that CGM acquired Gwandong, right?

39
04:23.853 --> 04:25.625
Yeah, I heard about that.

40
04:25.625 --> 04:28.613
Honestly, it kinda looks desperate.

41
04:28.613 --> 04:31.569
After their Korean launch flopped, they can't just leave with nothing.

42
04:31.569 --> 04:34.749
So they're buying a company just to make it

43
04:34.749 --> 04:36.633
look like they made it in, right?

44
04:36.633 --> 04:42.277
Gwandong already carried CGM's products, so not much has changed.

45
04:42.277 --> 04:44.225
From Gwandong's point of view, it's a pretty good deal.

46
04:44.225 --> 04:45.783
The company was on the verge of collapse,

47
04:45.783 --> 04:48.449
and they sold their stake at a good price.

48
04:48.449 --> 04:50.593
CGM really gave a lot of companies a hard time.

49
04:50.593 --> 04:53.937
They just pitted us against each other.

50
04:53.937 --> 04:58.589
It wasn't much of a fight. We were the only ones taking hits, right?

51
04:58.589 --> 05:01.933
We didn't even do anything.

52
05:09.845 --> 05:12.081
Since you brought it up,

53
05:12.081 --> 05:14.877
this wasn't a fight between your company and ours.

54
05:14.877 --> 05:18.441
In fact, pitting the vendors against each other over the commission rates,

55
05:18.441 --> 05:20.900
I believe, was your doing.

56
05:26.741 --> 05:28.893
You're Team Leader Gong Eun Tae, correct?

57
05:28.893 --> 05:30.537
Yes.

58
05:30.537 --> 05:33.549
He's the one who brought Mantua to Korea this time.

59
05:33.549 --> 05:36.900
Oh, I see.

60
05:38.149 --> 05:40.789
At the end of the day, it's business, isn't it?

61
05:40.789 --> 05:44.897
I hope you understand that we had no choice.

62
05:44.897 --> 05:47.721
When multiple companies want the same space,

63
05:47.721 --> 05:50.841
they're bound to compete.

64
05:50.841 --> 05:53.837
Yes, we fully understand that point.

65
05:53.837 --> 05:57.433
I'm sure Mr. Gong understands that too.

66
05:59.689 --> 06:01.697
What I'd like to ask is,

67
06:01.697 --> 06:05.549
whether Hongsung will take over the brands Gwandong used to carry,

68
06:05.549 --> 06:08.573
or leave them with Gwandong.

69
06:08.573 --> 06:11.425
What's Hongsung's take on this?

70
06:11.425 --> 06:13.700
[What's Hongsung's take on this?]

71
06:15.425 --> 06:18.197
We don't plan to take all the brands

72
06:18.197 --> 06:20.721
that overlap between Mantua and CGM.

73
06:20.721 --> 06:24.945
Especially if it's a brand they are already handling in Gwandong.

74
06:24.945 --> 06:28.653
We don't want Gwandong to disappear either.

75
06:28.653 --> 06:33.193
The market is more stable when major players stay in the game.

76
06:33.193 --> 06:37.641
Oh, I'm glad you see it that way.

77
06:37.641 --> 06:42.569
As you said, we'd also like to see Gwandong stay in business.

78
06:42.569 --> 06:47.233
But I don't quite understand why you keep bringing up

79
06:47.233 --> 06:49.949
Gwandong in particular.

80
06:49.949 --> 06:54.385
As you said, we're also partly responsible for this situation.

81
06:54.385 --> 06:59.900
We'd like to prevent any unnecessary competition.

82
07:01.357 --> 07:05.165
Of course, Hongsung won't go along with us.

83
07:05.165 --> 07:08.361
That's why we should strike first.

84
07:08.361 --> 07:12.581
But what if Hongsung actually pulls all its stores?

85
07:12.581 --> 07:14.168
No matter how big Hongsung is,

86
07:14.168 --> 07:16.901
how is it supposed to sell clothes without department stores?

87
07:16.901 --> 07:18.766
We need to come down hard.

88
07:19.421 --> 07:24.917
Look, if this blows up, it's over for both of us.

89
07:24.917 --> 07:27.000
Just do something.

90
07:28.689 --> 07:30.733
So, here's what we're thinking.

91
07:30.733 --> 07:34.649
For the brands that overlap between Hongsung and Gwandong in our select shop,

92
07:34.649 --> 07:38.965
how about we source a few of them from Gwandong too?

93
07:38.965 --> 07:40.833
What do you think?

94
07:48.101 --> 07:50.600
What do you think, Mr. Gong?

95
07:52.365 --> 07:54.500
Oh, personally,

96
07:55.209 --> 07:57.941
I'd ask you to reconsider that.

97
07:57.941 --> 08:00.481
Pardon? May I ask why you feel that way?

98
08:00.481 --> 08:02.173
You're our client,

99
08:02.173 --> 08:05.105
so it's not our place to tell you what to decide.

100
08:05.105 --> 08:10.266
But the people at Mantua aren't exactly reasonable.

101
08:10.266 --> 08:14.581
So, are you saying Hongsung is fine, but Mantua isn't?

102
08:14.581 --> 08:17.729
Yes, because your company is already in China.

103
08:17.729 --> 08:19.785
If CGM tries to use Gwandong

104
08:19.785 --> 08:23.129
as a backdoor to enter your Chinese department stores,

105
08:23.129 --> 08:26.069
I don't think Mantua would just sit back and watch.

106
08:26.069 --> 08:29.161
If that happens, the traditional European luxury brands on the first floor

107
08:29.161 --> 08:34.309
might end up completely empty.

108
08:34.309 --> 08:37.117
Ms. Park and I will go with the flow.

109
08:37.117 --> 08:39.049
Mr. Jang, you just set the tone.

110
08:39.049 --> 08:40.769
I'll leave the fighting to you, Mr. Gong.

111
08:40.769 --> 08:42.021
Yes, understood, sir.

112
08:42.021 --> 08:44.097
- Mr. Gong. - Yes.

113
08:44.097 --> 08:46.661
Go wild, do whatever you want.

114
08:46.661 --> 08:48.517
Understood, sir.

115
08:48.517 --> 08:52.137
And if you plan to diversify your supply through Gwandong,

116
08:52.137 --> 08:56.365
we'll revert your store-entry commission to the standard rate.

117
08:56.365 --> 08:58.457
I hope you can understand this point.

118
08:58.457 --> 09:02.033
Wait, wasn't that Hongsung's offer in the first place?

119
09:02.033 --> 09:03.704
The original contract

120
09:03.704 --> 09:06.953
was for your select shops to carry only Hongsung's products.

121
09:06.953 --> 09:11.433
If you're changing the terms, shouldn't we change ours as well?

122
09:11.433 --> 09:16.029
And we'll lower our commission to 14% for luxury brands.

123
09:16.029 --> 09:17.693
Wait, 14%?

124
09:17.693 --> 09:20.297
I believe you were charging 16% before,

125
09:20.297 --> 09:23.429
and after all this CGM trouble, you jacked it up to 20%.

126
09:23.429 --> 09:25.613
You even demanded 22% from CGM.

127
09:25.613 --> 09:28.241
If you want to start carrying our products again,

128
09:28.241 --> 09:30.877
you'll have to match our 14%.

129
09:30.877 --> 09:32.781
Wait, that's a bit...

130
09:32.781 --> 09:37.737
We understand what your company did to us.

131
09:37.737 --> 09:41.345
So we'd appreciate the same understanding from you.

132
09:41.345 --> 09:43.666
At the end of the day, it's all business.

133
10:02.373 --> 10:05.125
- Oh, Manager! - How are you?

134
10:05.125 --> 10:07.217
Mr. Yang!

135
10:07.829 --> 10:09.966
Enjoy it nice and cold.

136
10:11.477 --> 10:14.169
What on earth is going on?

137
10:14.169 --> 10:17.257
Why keep pulling stores in and out when we were doing fine?

138
10:17.257 --> 10:20.509
Well, you know how business goes sometimes.

139
10:20.509 --> 10:23.769
It's fine if Paradis Mall and Hongsung are playing tug-of-war,

140
10:23.769 --> 10:27.045
but aren't we the ones having to move the merchandise around?

141
10:27.045 --> 10:28.893
I know, I know, Manager.

142
10:28.893 --> 10:30.657
That's why I'm working on something.

143
10:30.657 --> 10:32.269
When we renew the contract this time,

144
10:32.269 --> 10:36.521
I'm going to try to raise the managers' commissions.

145
10:36.521 --> 10:40.609
- Are you serious? - I may be a bit of a pain, but not a liar.

146
10:40.609 --> 10:42.901
Yeah, that's true.

147
10:42.901 --> 10:45.966
Oh, this should probably be changed.

148
10:46.789 --> 10:48.733
Alright, there we go.

149
10:55.225 --> 10:57.217
- Mr. Yang. - Yeah?

150
10:57.217 --> 10:59.033
Over there...

151
11:11.221 --> 11:14.400
What? Do you want to say something?

152
11:16.341 --> 11:19.309
If you have nothing to say, just go. I'm swamped here.

153
11:19.309 --> 11:21.166
I'm sorry!

154
11:24.025 --> 11:25.465
For what?

155
11:25.465 --> 11:28.533
Well, I mean...

156
11:28.533 --> 11:29.905
What exactly are you sorry for?

157
11:29.905 --> 11:31.169
Well, you know...

158
11:31.169 --> 11:34.609
I must've lost my head for a moment.

159
11:34.609 --> 11:35.953
I mean...

160
11:35.953 --> 11:40.957
As you know, when we opened the store, we relied heavily on Hongsung.

161
11:40.957 --> 11:44.229
I think I unconsciously felt we were always bending over backward for Hongsung.

162
11:44.229 --> 11:49.529
And I guess I let a lot of resentment build up.

163
11:49.529 --> 11:52.445
I understand why you were upset.

164
11:52.445 --> 11:54.600
I hope you can let it go!

165
11:58.489 --> 12:01.441
Well, first of all, thank you for apologizing.

166
12:01.441 --> 12:04.317
I wasn't exactly blameless either.

167
12:04.317 --> 12:08.733
Why don't we just call it even for that mess and move on?

168
12:08.733 --> 12:12.065
Oh, thank you. I really appreciate it.

169
12:12.065 --> 12:14.833
Oh, wait! In that case...

170
12:15.757 --> 12:21.433
Can we assume the contract will proceed as before?

171
12:22.533 --> 12:24.033
No, that's not happening.

172
12:24.033 --> 12:26.193
- Pardon? - We yelled and fought each other.

173
12:26.193 --> 12:29.365
I totally admit it, I was completely wrong.

174
12:29.365 --> 12:32.833
But the way Paradis Mall treated us back then

175
12:33.517 --> 12:35.693
was clearly out of line.

176
12:35.693 --> 12:38.233
Of course, contracts can always be renewed,

177
12:38.233 --> 12:41.725
and you can take advantage of a favorable situation.

178
12:41.725 --> 12:43.929
But the way you did it was too much.

179
12:43.929 --> 12:46.345
You can go now. I've got a lot of work to do.

180
12:46.345 --> 12:49.517
Please, I'm begging you, Mr. Yang.

181
12:49.517 --> 12:52.469
We also agreed to split

182
12:52.469 --> 12:57.129
the penalty payment to Hongsung 50/50 with CGM.

183
12:57.129 --> 13:00.766
At this rate, our company is really going under!

184
13:01.497 --> 13:04.445
That's for Paradis Mall to deal with.

185
13:04.445 --> 13:06.249
Companies don't go under that easily.

186
13:06.249 --> 13:07.901
I know. You won't go under.

187
13:07.901 --> 13:09.673
Mr. Yang!

188
13:09.673 --> 13:12.533
Please, I'm begging you.

189
13:13.301 --> 13:15.817
Oh, for god's sake!

190
13:15.817 --> 13:19.133
I'll even help carry boxes for you.

191
13:19.925 --> 13:22.029
Why would you carry boxes?

192
13:22.029 --> 13:24.609
Why would we make you do something so menial?

193
13:24.609 --> 13:26.029
Oh, jeez.

194
13:26.029 --> 13:29.281
Well, I noticed the store's interior looked pretty dated.

195
13:29.281 --> 13:33.105
Let's talk again about the interior design. Okay?

196
13:33.105 --> 13:34.973
Later, later. You can get on your knees later.

197
13:34.973 --> 13:36.266
No, no, later! I'll call you later.

198
13:36.266 --> 13:37.966
Oh, you're so heavy.

199
13:38.581 --> 13:41.366
Oh, okay. I'll call you.

200
13:42.749 --> 13:44.801
Jeez.

201
13:44.801 --> 13:48.100
Wait, Mr. Yang...

202
13:52.237 --> 13:54.113
Seriously...

203
13:55.617 --> 13:57.733
Darn it!

204
14:18.537 --> 14:19.909
Good work, everyone.

205
14:19.909 --> 14:21.353
Thank you for your hard work.

206
14:21.353 --> 14:22.993
Ms. Park, come up to my office.

207
14:22.993 --> 14:24.797
Yes, sir.

208
14:28.793 --> 14:30.005
Oh, dear.

209
14:30.005 --> 14:32.593
Go on ahead. I'll park the car and be right in.

210
14:32.593 --> 14:34.741
Alright.

211
14:34.741 --> 14:36.665
Good work.

212
15:06.845 --> 15:09.033
How did you get up here?

213
15:09.937 --> 15:11.157
It still works.

214
15:11.157 --> 15:12.949
[Jung Sun Hyuk]

215
15:15.266 --> 15:17.861
Strangely, I wanted to come up here.

216
15:17.861 --> 15:20.333
You have a nicer office now.

217
15:23.200 --> 15:26.865
I heard CGM acquired Gwandong.

218
15:26.865 --> 15:29.033
Are you working at Gwandong?

219
15:30.077 --> 15:31.821
America is great, I'll give them that.

220
15:31.821 --> 15:35.017
Even after I screwed things up that badly, they gave me another chance.

221
15:35.017 --> 15:37.821
So I'll be working at Gwandong for a while.

222
15:37.821 --> 15:39.700
That's great.

223
15:41.433 --> 15:44.697
You landed Mantua, didn't you?

224
15:44.697 --> 15:46.053
My team did it.

225
15:46.053 --> 15:49.101
Stop saying it like that. It's not a good look.

226
15:49.101 --> 15:51.466
You can just say you did it.

227
15:52.457 --> 15:55.329
Hongsung seems to have tightened its grip on the market.

228
15:55.329 --> 16:00.617
I saw you actually gave up some margin to the companies that stayed loyal.

229
16:00.617 --> 16:03.965
You sent a clear signal to the market.

230
16:03.965 --> 16:07.133
"Stick with Hongsung and you profit."

231
16:07.133 --> 16:10.581
"Go against Hongsung, and we'll fight back with everything we've got."

232
16:12.021 --> 16:14.201
Well, that wasn't really our intention.

233
16:14.201 --> 16:18.333
We were just expressing our gratitude in our own way.

234
16:19.777 --> 16:21.793
Honestly, you had fun, didn't you?

235
16:21.793 --> 16:23.166
With what?

236
16:23.166 --> 16:25.217
The work.

237
16:25.217 --> 16:27.289
You enjoyed it, didn't you?

238
16:27.289 --> 16:29.205
I can tell without asking.

239
16:29.205 --> 16:32.000
I even had fun though I lost.

240
16:33.573 --> 16:37.465
Leaving Hongsung makes me feel like I'm working again.

241
16:37.465 --> 16:40.785
So I don't really regret it.

242
16:40.785 --> 16:44.533
Why? Because I genuinely enjoy it.

243
16:45.233 --> 16:49.521
That's why I'm so jealous of you.

244
16:49.521 --> 16:54.266
It took me leaving to find it, but you found it without leaving.

245
16:56.057 --> 17:00.513
I do enjoy the work.

246
17:00.513 --> 17:04.766
But I think my takeaway is a bit different.

247
17:05.633 --> 17:09.145
As you said, the company went through a major crisis,

248
17:09.145 --> 17:12.433
and I enjoyed overcoming it.

249
17:13.401 --> 17:17.449
Besides the excitement of the job itself,

250
17:17.449 --> 17:20.977
I felt incredibly lonely when I got home.

251
17:20.977 --> 17:24.865
How should I put it? If I'm being a bit dramatic,

252
17:24.865 --> 17:28.966
it felt like I saved the world and nobody even knew.

253
17:29.981 --> 17:31.661
That's how life is, I guess.

254
17:31.661 --> 17:34.900
What's important to me isn't necessarily important to others.

255
17:36.317 --> 17:38.293
But then, out of nowhere,

256
17:39.797 --> 17:42.700
I suddenly started missing everyone from the office so much.

257
17:43.569 --> 17:45.966
Come on, I'm serious.

258
17:46.989 --> 17:48.866
We know, right?

259
17:49.581 --> 17:51.725
What we did

260
17:51.725 --> 17:53.833
and how we did it.

261
17:53.833 --> 17:58.066
How we came up with ideas and how much we agonized over them.

262
17:59.233 --> 18:03.000
How we fought and negotiated.

263
18:06.345 --> 18:08.945
How anxious we were.

264
18:08.945 --> 18:11.100
How hard it was,

265
18:11.965 --> 18:14.066
and how happy we were.

266
18:16.089 --> 18:20.800
I realized how grateful I am to have colleagues who share it all with me.

267
18:21.889 --> 18:24.093
So these days,

268
18:24.093 --> 18:26.000
I just enjoy that feeling.

269
18:27.641 --> 18:29.717
Eun Tae,

270
18:30.993 --> 18:33.466
was I ever that kind of person for you?

271
18:39.161 --> 18:43.873
I don't think you ever have to cut someone off.

272
18:43.873 --> 18:49.066
I think the right distance changes with time and people.

273
18:50.749 --> 18:52.465
Sometime later,

274
18:52.465 --> 18:54.900
once a bit more time has passed,

275
18:54.900 --> 18:59.800
let's grab a drink, just like we used to. How about it?

276
19:01.765 --> 19:03.241
Sounds good, Mr. Jung.

277
19:03.241 --> 19:04.633
Good.

278
19:04.633 --> 19:06.509
Darn it.

279
19:06.509 --> 19:07.957
Mind if I have another cigarette?

280
19:07.957 --> 19:10.241
Why are you asking me for permission?

281
19:10.241 --> 19:12.066
It's your company.

282
19:17.893 --> 19:20.100
- Mr. Jung. - Yeah?

283
19:20.761 --> 19:23.900
Do you still play the lottery?

284
19:25.201 --> 19:27.129
Do you?

285
19:33.509 --> 19:35.917
Honestly, wasn't that a bit much?

286
19:35.917 --> 19:39.493
I understand security is important, but shutting me out like that?

287
19:39.493 --> 19:41.325
I'm sorry, sir.

288
19:42.441 --> 19:44.165
Don't be.

289
19:44.165 --> 19:46.966
You'd do the exact same thing all over again, wouldn't you?

290
19:47.941 --> 19:50.309
Jeez, seriously.

291
19:50.309 --> 19:52.241
How old is your kid now?

292
19:52.241 --> 19:54.133
She's in high school.

293
19:55.301 --> 19:57.866
You did a great job raising her while working so hard.

294
19:57.866 --> 19:59.981
I didn't do much.

295
19:59.981 --> 20:01.493
She pretty much raised herself.

296
20:01.493 --> 20:04.541
You'll need to make good money to send her to college.

297
20:04.541 --> 20:08.100
Yes. That's why I work hard.

298
20:08.905 --> 20:12.425
You know executives get full tuition for their kids, right?

299
20:12.425 --> 20:14.405
Pardon?

300
20:17.577 --> 20:19.521
Let's go for the director position.

301
20:22.957 --> 20:25.229
We'll merge Sales Divisions 1 and 2

302
20:25.229 --> 20:27.417
and create a Sales Director position.

303
20:27.417 --> 20:29.333
You'll also have a Sales Planning Department reporting directly to you.

304
20:29.333 --> 20:32.497
[Organizational Restructuring, Personnel Changes]

305
20:32.497 --> 20:35.061
Go on, give it your best.

306
20:35.061 --> 20:36.833
Understood, sir.

307
20:37.453 --> 20:39.153
Hey.

308
20:39.153 --> 20:40.645
Yes?

309
20:40.645 --> 20:42.633
Aren't you going to say thank you?

310
20:45.065 --> 20:47.361
Thank you, sir.

311
20:47.361 --> 20:49.366
Jeez.

312
20:54.561 --> 20:57.233
[HR Notice, Personnel Changes and Organizational Restructuring]

313
21:02.029 --> 21:03.721
[Personnel Changes]

314
21:03.721 --> 21:07.066
[Gong Eun Tae, Deputy Director of Sales Strategy]

315
21:16.577 --> 21:20.005
Congratulations, Mr. Gong.

316
21:20.005 --> 21:21.805
Mr. Yang,

317
21:22.433 --> 21:23.877
congratulations.

318
21:23.877 --> 21:25.677
What?

319
21:26.400 --> 21:30.366
[Yang Jun Ho, Sales Manager]

320
21:56.969 --> 21:58.073
Congratulations, Mr. Oh.

321
21:58.073 --> 21:59.585
Oh, no.

322
21:59.585 --> 22:03.966
Oh, I'm absolutely the type to get all worked up over a promotion.

323
22:03.966 --> 22:05.557
- Jeez. - Oh, my.

324
22:05.557 --> 22:08.129
- Congratulations! - What's there to congratulate me for?

325
22:08.129 --> 22:10.433
- I really mean it. Congratulations. - No, no.

326
22:10.433 --> 22:11.901
Congratulations, Deputy Director.

327
22:11.901 --> 22:14.266
- Oh, thank you. - Congratulations.

328
22:17.745 --> 22:19.633
Everyone in Sales Team 5,

329
22:20.401 --> 22:22.933
you've got ten minutes to wrap up your work.

330
22:32.317 --> 22:35.809
Oh, Deputy Director Gong, let me make you a drink this time.

331
22:35.809 --> 22:38.717
Wait, you shouldn't be doing this.

332
22:38.717 --> 22:41.665
Come on, I'll make the drink you like...

333
22:41.665 --> 22:43.601
Oh, what the heck? We're out of all the cold stuff.

334
22:43.601 --> 22:44.881
I'll go grab some, Team Leader Yang.

335
22:44.881 --> 22:46.707
Ji Hye, you need to grill the meat.

336
22:46.707 --> 22:48.525
Why are you trying to do everything yourself?

337
22:48.525 --> 22:50.077
Gi Tae, what are you doing right now?

338
22:50.077 --> 22:52.345
Team Leader, let me just finish this, and I'll go get them.

339
22:52.345 --> 22:53.413
I'll do it, Team Leader.

340
22:53.413 --> 22:55.653
Oh, Team Leader, please sit down. It's all done, all done.

341
22:55.653 --> 22:58.057
She's an assistant manager. The team leader is right here.

342
22:58.057 --> 23:00.357
Oh, I'm sorry, Team Leader.

343
23:00.357 --> 23:02.749
Oh, come on!

344
23:02.749 --> 23:05.133
Deputy Director, please!

345
23:16.657 --> 23:18.701
Here, take this. You said it's good for your stomach.

346
23:18.701 --> 23:21.466
[Stomach Health Supplement]

347
23:27.965 --> 23:30.889
After all these years at the company, I guess I've earned a day like this.

348
23:30.889 --> 23:33.493
There really aren't any days when everything is just good.

349
23:33.493 --> 23:35.153
I know.

350
23:35.153 --> 23:37.413
Our team really did well, didn't we?

351
23:37.413 --> 23:39.209
Well, this is all because of...

352
23:40.269 --> 23:41.453
It's all thanks to you, Team Leader.

353
23:41.453 --> 23:44.553
Oh, please, it's thanks to you, Deputy Director.

354
23:44.553 --> 23:48.200
Wow, this is hilarious, just us talking like this.

355
23:49.529 --> 23:55.185
I think all of this happened because you got mad at me that day.

356
23:55.185 --> 23:59.965
Come to think of it, our team's success started then too.

357
23:59.965 --> 24:03.889
If you hadn't gotten mad at me that day

358
24:03.889 --> 24:06.137
and just let it slide,

359
24:06.137 --> 24:08.921
I don't think we'd be here now.

360
24:08.921 --> 24:11.766
Thank you for getting mad at me.

361
24:18.153 --> 24:20.125
By the way,

362
24:20.125 --> 24:22.425
what will happen to Ji Hye?

363
24:22.425 --> 24:24.529
Our team's results are good,

364
24:24.529 --> 24:27.765
and her team leader's review should be good too.

365
24:27.765 --> 24:29.369
But I'm still worried.

366
24:29.369 --> 24:32.769
I've talked to the other team leaders,

367
24:32.769 --> 24:34.409
but I don't know how it'll turn out.

368
24:34.409 --> 24:36.500
Oh, it's done. Here, eat.

369
24:37.785 --> 24:40.949
We've done everything we can, so we just have to wait and see.

370
24:40.949 --> 24:42.901
Isn't there anything we can do?

371
24:42.901 --> 24:45.233
I just can't put my mind at ease.

372
25:04.529 --> 25:06.449
Keep up the good work.

373
25:06.449 --> 25:10.861
- What brings you here? - I'm supposed to meet someone inside here.

374
25:10.861 --> 25:13.566
You can't just walk in here like this.

375
25:26.149 --> 25:28.869
Yes, this is the Executive Director's office.

376
25:28.869 --> 25:30.069
Yes.

377
25:30.069 --> 25:31.933
Wait, what?

378
25:36.145 --> 25:37.909
Seriously, he's...

379
25:40.721 --> 25:43.933
- CEO? - What? Why are you working?

380
25:43.933 --> 25:46.409
Well, it's work hours. What else would I be doing?

381
25:46.409 --> 25:51.069
You could've practiced putting. Then my visit would've been worth it.

382
25:51.069 --> 25:54.333
I put it away in case you came.

383
25:54.333 --> 25:55.809
Get me a cup of coffee.

384
25:55.809 --> 25:57.561
Sure. What kind of coffee would you like?

385
25:57.561 --> 26:00.221
Ethiopian Yirgacheffe.

386
26:00.221 --> 26:01.433
Just give him an instant coffee.

387
26:01.433 --> 26:03.229
Yes, sir.

388
26:04.641 --> 26:07.029
What brings you here without notice?

389
26:07.029 --> 26:09.593
Why would I call before coming to my own company?

390
26:09.593 --> 26:11.821
It just puts me on edge.

391
26:11.821 --> 26:12.953
Fair point.

392
26:12.953 --> 26:14.729
Yeah.

393
26:15.409 --> 26:17.437
I saw the personnel changes.

394
26:17.437 --> 26:19.597
There were the issues with Sales Division 2,

395
26:19.597 --> 26:21.241
and the Mantua order situation,

396
26:21.241 --> 26:23.489
so I made the changes with the restructuring.

397
26:23.489 --> 26:26.217
Companies are really something else, huh?

398
26:26.217 --> 26:30.741
Just when you think everything's perfect and you don't need to touch a thing,

399
26:30.741 --> 26:33.493
a problem comes up.

400
26:33.493 --> 26:34.645
That's because people run them.

401
26:34.645 --> 26:37.201
Yeah, but then again,

402
26:37.201 --> 26:39.766
when you think it's all over, and there's no coming back,

403
26:39.766 --> 26:43.729
somehow, some way, things work out.

404
26:43.729 --> 26:45.105
That's because people run them.

405
26:45.105 --> 26:47.166
I suppose that's true.

406
26:47.869 --> 26:50.981
By the way, is that Team Leader Gong any good?

407
26:50.981 --> 26:52.937
I'm keeping a close eye on him.

408
26:52.937 --> 26:56.433
I'd like to meet him. Send him up.

409
26:59.649 --> 27:01.533
- Gong Eun Tae! - Yes?

410
27:01.533 --> 27:02.741
The CEO wants to see you.

411
27:02.741 --> 27:05.261
- Pardon? - The CEO asked for you. Get up here fast.

412
27:05.261 --> 27:07.033
Oh, yes, sir.

413
27:11.137 --> 27:13.966
But why would the CEO want to see me?

414
27:14.593 --> 27:16.941
How would I know?

415
27:16.941 --> 27:19.369
What, are you nervous?

416
27:19.369 --> 27:23.066
No, but you seem to be the one who's nervous.

417
27:25.241 --> 27:27.181
Have you ever met the CEO?

418
27:27.181 --> 27:30.025
No. I only saw him from a distance at the New Year's party.

419
27:30.025 --> 27:31.841
He never comes to the office, right?

420
27:31.841 --> 27:33.569
Yes, that's what I've heard.

421
27:33.569 --> 27:38.166
I've never known him to show up unannounced and call someone in.

422
27:38.825 --> 27:40.629
This is a first.

423
27:43.849 --> 27:47.200
Have you ever met him, sir?

424
27:49.737 --> 27:51.905
Once, during a strategy meeting for the duty-free business.

425
27:51.905 --> 27:53.761
What was he like?

426
27:55.921 --> 27:59.541
At first, he came off as a bit sloppy, I guess.

427
27:59.541 --> 28:03.017
But as the meeting went on, I realized,

428
28:03.017 --> 28:06.266
he is not the kind of man I can ever judge.

429
28:09.245 --> 28:12.721
Take it easy. You're as good as dead anyway.

430
28:12.721 --> 28:14.933
Door opens.

431
28:18.185 --> 28:20.065
Go on in.

432
28:41.385 --> 28:42.973
Is that him?

433
28:42.973 --> 28:45.189
- Yes, sir. - Yeah.

434
28:45.189 --> 28:47.021
Come on in, please.

435
28:49.089 --> 28:50.845
Right over here.

436
28:50.845 --> 28:52.761
Oh, yes, sir.

437
29:07.181 --> 29:09.597
You're quite a fine-looking young man!

438
29:09.597 --> 29:12.421
Oh, thank you, sir.

439
29:12.421 --> 29:14.466
I hear you've been working hard.

440
29:14.466 --> 29:16.589
Congrats on the promotion to Deputy Director.

441
29:16.589 --> 29:18.773
Thank you, sir.

442
29:18.773 --> 29:23.037
You know I don't come to the office much, right?

443
29:25.000 --> 29:28.021
I heard you have more important things to do outside the office.

444
29:28.021 --> 29:30.993
Oh, you sweet talker.

445
29:30.993 --> 29:33.677
No, I'm just playing around.

446
29:33.677 --> 29:38.337
I didn't come here because I got bored of having fun.

447
29:38.337 --> 29:41.853
I wanted to give you a gift, Mr. Gong.

448
29:41.853 --> 29:44.685
From what I've heard, you deserve one.

449
29:44.685 --> 29:48.537
Pick out a promotion gift for yourself.

450
29:48.537 --> 29:50.925
What kind of gift are you talking about, sir?

451
29:50.925 --> 29:53.966
Anything within my authority.

452
30:24.069 --> 30:25.977
Mr. Gong,

453
30:27.177 --> 30:29.133
what did he call you in for?

454
30:31.573 --> 30:34.049
Oh, just tell me. Anything at all.

455
30:34.049 --> 30:36.341
Anything's fine. Really.

456
30:36.341 --> 30:38.800
Are you sure that's okay, sir?

457
30:43.849 --> 30:45.641
Sir,

458
30:45.641 --> 30:50.105
we have a contract employee named Lee Ji Hye.

459
30:50.105 --> 30:52.381
If I can really

460
30:52.381 --> 30:54.557
choose my gift,

461
30:54.557 --> 30:57.900
I'd like to make her a permanent employee.

462
31:00.517 --> 31:04.789
Is this Ms. Lee Ji Hye good at her job?

463
31:04.789 --> 31:10.366
Yes, sir. She played a big part in securing our contract with Mantua.

464
31:12.313 --> 31:15.200
So she's good at her job, huh?

465
31:16.973 --> 31:18.941
That's a shame.

466
31:20.905 --> 31:25.981
Someone that good would've become permanent without you asking.

467
31:25.981 --> 31:29.233
- Sir. - Oh, hold on.

468
31:30.666 --> 31:32.329
Mr. Gong, listen carefully.

469
31:32.329 --> 31:33.565
Yes, sir.

470
31:33.565 --> 31:35.441
I'm going to

471
31:36.217 --> 31:38.500
fire her.

472
31:48.713 --> 31:52.833
[HR, Contract Termination Notice Posted]

473
31:57.200 --> 32:04.166
[Notice of Contract Termination, Lee Ji Hye]

474
32:06.105 --> 32:08.900
What is that supposed to mean?

475
32:09.505 --> 32:13.497
I gave you authority, Mr. Gong.

476
32:13.497 --> 32:17.509
That was your first task as a Deputy Director.

477
32:17.509 --> 32:19.466
You could've used that authority

478
32:19.466 --> 32:22.149
to change unfair policies

479
32:22.149 --> 32:24.197
or restructure the organization.

480
32:24.197 --> 32:27.777
You could've given Sales the authority to handle matters

481
32:27.777 --> 32:31.400
that once required Finance and Legal approval.

482
32:31.400 --> 32:37.645
And all you did with that authority was make a contract worker permanent?

483
32:37.645 --> 32:42.517
Well, I thought she was essential to our company.

484
32:42.517 --> 32:43.866
Well, then,

485
32:43.866 --> 32:48.933
you should've used your rank to change the HR system, so you could do that.

486
32:48.933 --> 32:53.566
That's how a manager should think.

487
32:54.489 --> 33:00.666
Good grief. My gift to you this time is that person, Lee Ji Hye,

488
33:00.666 --> 33:02.677
will be fired.

489
33:02.677 --> 33:06.833
I hope this gift teaches you something.

490
33:18.885 --> 33:21.417
I'm sorry. I...

491
33:21.417 --> 33:22.913
I shouldn't have brought it up.

492
33:22.913 --> 33:25.705
No, don't be, Mr. Gong. I'm really okay.

493
33:25.705 --> 33:27.301
What's okay about this?

494
33:27.301 --> 33:29.266
We're not okay with it either.

495
33:34.765 --> 33:37.441
Mr. Gong, do you remember this?

496
33:37.441 --> 33:38.853
What's that?

497
33:38.853 --> 33:44.466
These are the materials I made when Ms. Jang first joined us.

498
33:45.833 --> 33:50.189
You put them on a USB and gave it to me.

499
33:50.189 --> 33:51.993
You said no matter what happened,

500
33:51.993 --> 33:56.666
it wouldn't change my value as the person who made them.

501
33:57.813 --> 34:00.197
So I'm really okay with this.

502
34:00.197 --> 34:02.333
A year as a contract worker at Hongsung

503
34:02.333 --> 34:06.445
is more than enough experience for other companies to value.

504
34:06.445 --> 34:08.365
And,

505
34:09.017 --> 34:13.105
I think I had a great time with a great team.

506
34:13.105 --> 34:16.733
So please, don't be like this. I'm truly okay.

507
34:18.225 --> 34:22.569
Well, after a year at Hongsung, you've got nothing to be ashamed of.

508
34:22.569 --> 34:23.633
Of course.

509
34:23.633 --> 34:26.166
Ji Hye, you'll do well no matter what you do.

510
34:26.166 --> 34:29.785
Whether you work part-time or go abroad.

511
34:29.785 --> 34:30.813
Right, Mr. Gong?

512
34:30.813 --> 34:32.497
Tell me about it.

513
34:32.497 --> 34:34.300
Speaking of which,

514
34:34.997 --> 34:39.066
have you ever considered working abroad?

515
34:40.849 --> 34:44.017
What? Working abroad?

516
34:44.017 --> 34:47.166
How about Mantua?

517
34:49.221 --> 34:51.629
Mantua?

518
34:51.629 --> 34:53.600
Isn't there another way?

519
34:55.101 --> 34:59.333
I'm confident Ji Hye will become permanent.

520
34:59.333 --> 35:01.781
But if that doesn't happen,

521
35:01.781 --> 35:04.353
how about sending her to Mantua?

522
35:04.353 --> 35:05.589
Mantua?

523
35:05.589 --> 35:08.705
Yeah, I didn't just put her in charge

524
35:08.705 --> 35:11.273
of dealing with Mantua for no reason.

525
35:11.273 --> 35:14.401
Mantua will be sending more goods to Korea,

526
35:14.401 --> 35:16.789
so they'll probably need someone dedicated to it.

527
35:16.789 --> 35:18.645
What do you think?

528
35:18.645 --> 35:20.533
Mr. Gong.

529
35:21.273 --> 35:22.997
It's too sudden, right?

530
35:22.997 --> 35:25.809
Just think about it, and let me know.

531
35:25.809 --> 35:30.413
But would Mantua even want me?

532
35:30.413 --> 35:33.133
Just think about whether you'd like it.

533
35:34.069 --> 35:36.633
If you're willing,

534
35:38.297 --> 35:40.166
Mr. Sponza said

535
35:41.289 --> 35:43.466
you'd be more than welcome.

536
35:45.757 --> 35:48.566
Mr. Gong!

537
35:52.577 --> 35:54.129
Are you crying again?

538
35:54.129 --> 35:57.761
What? You don't cry when you're sad, but you cry when you're happy?

539
35:57.761 --> 36:01.300
- Forget it. - That was mean.

540
36:02.261 --> 36:06.233
Oh, so being pampered makes you hit people now?

541
36:07.357 --> 36:12.166
Let's give her some time alone.

542
36:13.033 --> 36:16.129
- Go cry it out. - Where are you guys going?

543
36:16.129 --> 36:18.497
Wait for me!

544
36:18.497 --> 36:22.537
Ms. Ji Hye is going to Mantua?

545
36:22.537 --> 36:23.873
Thankfully, she seemed excited about it.

546
36:23.873 --> 36:27.341
That's great. It's a much bigger company.

547
36:27.341 --> 36:29.709
Well, she speaks Italian well too.

548
36:29.709 --> 36:31.933
- Right. - She'll adjust just fine, right?

549
36:31.933 --> 36:33.737
Of course.

550
36:33.737 --> 36:37.081
What is there to worry about? She'll manage on her own now.

551
36:37.081 --> 36:39.200
- You think so? - Yeah.

552
36:42.713 --> 36:44.369
Hey,

553
36:44.369 --> 36:48.053
don't you think people have changed?

554
36:48.053 --> 36:50.373
Why, what's changed?

555
36:50.373 --> 36:55.741
Well, I can't say for sure that you have.

556
36:55.741 --> 36:58.333
But I also can't say you haven't.

557
37:01.281 --> 37:04.313
I don't know about that.

558
37:04.313 --> 37:06.409
Have I ever said that to you?

559
37:06.409 --> 37:07.521
What?

560
37:07.521 --> 37:10.933
Back with Yoo Ji Hyun, and the whole CGM thing,

561
37:11.561 --> 37:13.533
did I ever say

562
37:14.605 --> 37:16.766
thank you?

563
37:17.393 --> 37:19.277
Thank me?

564
37:19.277 --> 37:20.977
You?

565
37:20.977 --> 37:22.901
Did you?

566
37:26.369 --> 37:28.166
I guess I didn't.

567
37:31.633 --> 37:33.469
Thanks.

568
37:38.365 --> 37:40.281
I'm off.

569
37:47.105 --> 37:48.965
You've changed.

570
38:55.633 --> 39:00.333
[Daily Routine]

571
39:03.585 --> 39:05.333
Oh.

572
39:08.629 --> 39:10.977
Today's beans have a bit of acidity.

573
39:10.977 --> 39:12.817
Sounds nice.

574
39:13.673 --> 39:15.149
Well, sir,

575
39:15.149 --> 39:18.257
you remember the espresso pack we took with us last time?

576
39:18.257 --> 39:20.725
Sure, I remember.

577
39:20.725 --> 39:24.941
The person who drank it said,

578
39:24.941 --> 39:28.661
"This coffee wasn't made for someone else."

579
39:28.661 --> 39:30.777
That's quite something.

580
39:30.777 --> 39:35.513
Because you know, coffee reflects the person who makes it.

581
39:35.513 --> 39:38.329
That's fascinating. That's exactly what she said.

582
39:38.329 --> 39:41.897
I do make coffee for others.

583
39:41.897 --> 39:47.433
But I like seeing someone enjoy my coffee, so in the end, it's for me too.

584
39:52.209 --> 39:54.201
Well, sir.

585
39:54.201 --> 39:57.500
This may be a little out of the blue,

586
39:59.417 --> 40:01.466
but did you perhaps...

587
40:02.069 --> 40:04.065
Did I perhaps

588
40:05.709 --> 40:08.125
win the lottery?

589
40:08.125 --> 40:10.261
You did, didn't you?

590
40:10.261 --> 40:12.345
Is it that obvious?

591
40:12.345 --> 40:15.193
I don't know what it is, but I just had a feeling.

592
40:15.193 --> 40:17.921
I know, right? I could tell too.

593
40:17.921 --> 40:19.966
So you already knew.

594
40:21.045 --> 40:24.100
So what's it like having all that money in the bank?

595
40:25.237 --> 40:27.013
I don't know.

596
40:29.609 --> 40:32.033
I haven't spent a single cent of it,

597
40:33.077 --> 40:37.166
but it showed me that so many things could still change.

598
40:38.433 --> 40:41.089
Then again,

599
40:41.089 --> 40:43.166
maybe I could

600
40:44.309 --> 40:47.345
live this same life, even without the money.

601
40:48.625 --> 40:52.666
I thought nothing had changed at all, but looking back,

602
40:54.429 --> 40:56.733
everything had changed.

603
40:57.617 --> 40:59.469
I guess so.

604
41:00.421 --> 41:03.166
Just like the taste of coffee changes every day.

605
41:04.481 --> 41:06.600
Have a good day.

606
41:07.917 --> 41:08.969
You too, sir.

607
41:08.969 --> 41:11.277
Thanks, see you tomorrow.

608
41:11.277 --> 41:12.313
See you tomorrow.

609
41:12.313 --> 41:17.066
[Daily Routine]

610
41:24.165 --> 41:27.285
I'm still the same as yesterday,

611
41:27.285 --> 41:30.100
living a day that will be the same as tomorrow.

612
41:31.289 --> 41:36.466
And just like that, time continues to pass by, casually, even today.

613
42:03.277 --> 42:05.333
Door closes.

614
42:08.201 --> 42:10.161
Door opens.

615
42:10.161 --> 42:12.117
Oh, my.

616
42:12.117 --> 42:15.433
- You're here. - I really thought I was first.

617
42:16.405 --> 42:17.881
Good morning, good morning.

618
42:17.881 --> 42:19.073
Ms. Jang!

619
42:19.073 --> 42:20.421
You're all here early.

620
42:20.421 --> 42:21.905
Of course.

621
42:21.905 --> 42:23.209
- Oh, good morning. - Good morning.

622
42:23.209 --> 42:26.349
- Good morning. - Wow, everyone's right on time now.

623
42:26.349 --> 42:28.473
What's going on? Why are you two coming in together?

624
42:28.473 --> 42:30.309
Oh...

625
42:31.957 --> 42:34.100
Door closes.

626
43:04.565 --> 43:05.633
Hello.

627
43:05.633 --> 43:09.533
[Draw Date: August 22, 1st Place Winner, Congratulations]

628
43:15.193 --> 43:18.113
Sorry, but our POS system isn't working.

629
43:19.797 --> 43:21.417
Luckily, I have cash.

630
43:21.417 --> 43:23.900
Okay, got your 10,000 won.

631
43:26.141 --> 43:27.837
But you don't have any change, right?

632
43:27.837 --> 43:29.766
Yeah, you're right.

633
43:32.833 --> 43:34.800
How would you like me to handle this?
